        ":question/id": "f11bb3fa-ce88-546d-aefd-7cd344d3c36f",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int {e}^{\\frac{x}{7} - 4}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=\\frac{x}{7} - 4,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{7}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=7\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{\\frac{x}{7} - 4}\\,\\text{d}x&=\\int 1{e}^{u}\\cdot 7\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=7\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &=7{e}^{u}+C \\\\ &=7 {e}^{\\frac{x}{7} - 4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
